A good hospital:

1. is **clean**, well ventilated and has good drainage and proper **waste disposal**;
2. has **enough qualified staff** (doctors, nurses, laboratory technicians, pharmacists);
3. has **adequate equipment**, a laboratory and a **supply of drugs**;
4. is easily **accessible** (good roads, central location) and quiet, away from noise and pollution;
5. has a **constant supply of water and electricity**;
6. has **separate wards** (maternity, children, isolation ward for infectious diseases) and **emergency services** such as an ambulance;
7. offers **affordable services**, respects patients' privacy and has a good attitude toward patients.

(Any six.)
